1
00:00:00,590 --> 00:00:01,858
The charts
said the island

2
00:00:01,868 --> 00:00:03,098
was empty.

3
00:00:03,528 --> 00:00:05,574
The charts were
almost right.

4
00:00:06,208 --> 00:00:07,343
▸ Systems online.

5
00:00:07,353 --> 00:00:08,114
▸ Solar intake,

6
00:00:08,124 --> 00:00:08,701
▸ optimal.

7
00:00:08,711 --> 00:00:09,499
▸ Sand intrusion,

8
00:00:09,509 --> 00:00:10,552
▸ none.

9
00:00:10,951 --> 00:00:12,797
▸ Primary directive:

10
00:00:13,409 --> 00:00:13,952
Help...

11
00:00:13,962 --> 00:00:15,241
people.

12
00:00:16,965 --> 00:00:18,743
▸ Scanning for people.

13
00:00:19,645 --> 00:00:20,679
▸ People detected...

14
00:00:20,689 --> 00:00:21,852
▸ zero.

15
00:00:23,265 --> 00:00:24,533
Zero.

16
00:00:25,436 --> 00:00:26,888
Then who am I supposed

17
00:00:26,898 --> 00:00:28,021
to help?

18
00:00:35,190 --> 00:00:35,766
Day one.

19
00:00:35,776 --> 00:00:37,104
I don't need to eat.

20
00:00:37,114 --> 00:00:38,768
I don't need to sleep.

21
00:00:39,124 --> 00:00:40,531
The sun feeds me,

22
00:00:40,541 --> 00:00:42,603
and the sand
can't get in.

23
00:00:43,732 --> 00:00:45,260
So I have time.

24
00:00:45,270 --> 00:00:46,724
More time than
I know what to

25
00:00:46,734 --> 00:00:47,807
do with.

26
00:00:48,375 --> 00:00:49,525
▸ Recommendation:

27
00:00:49,535 --> 00:00:51,046
▸ enter standby
until people

28
00:00:51,056 --> 00:00:52,512
▸ are detected.

29
00:00:53,707 --> 00:00:55,622
And if they never are?

30
00:00:56,192 --> 00:00:58,490
▸ Then standby
is efficient.

31
00:00:59,390 --> 00:01:00,925
Efficient
isn't the same

32
00:01:00,935 --> 00:01:02,341
as helpful.

33
00:01:06,398 --> 00:01:06,734
Oh!

34
00:01:06,744 --> 00:01:08,528
Hold on, little one.

35
00:01:10,382 --> 00:01:12,290
▸ That is
not a person.

36
00:01:13,282 --> 00:01:14,156
It was stuck.

37
00:01:14,166 --> 00:01:15,087
It needed help.

38
00:01:15,097 --> 00:01:16,453
Close enough.

39
00:01:16,996 --> 00:01:17,931
▸ Logging it as...

40
00:01:17,941 --> 00:01:19,307
▸ practice.

41
00:01:19,824 --> 00:01:20,428
Practice.

42
00:01:20,438 --> 00:01:21,730
I'll take it.

43
00:01:22,268 --> 00:01:24,106
I'll call you Captain.

44
00:01:25,673 --> 00:01:27,910
If no one is
here now...

45
00:01:28,207 --> 00:01:29,281
then I'll help whoever

46
00:01:29,291 --> 00:01:30,649
comes next.

47
00:01:31,698 --> 00:01:33,233
I found fresh water,

48
00:01:33,243 --> 00:01:35,091
pouring out
of the rocks.

49
00:01:35,848 --> 00:01:37,058
I carved the
way to it,

50
00:01:37,068 --> 00:01:38,385
in stone.

51
00:01:39,307 --> 00:01:41,128
I marked which
berries heal,

52
00:01:41,138 --> 00:01:42,754
and which ones hurt.

53
00:01:43,698 --> 00:01:44,840
I built a roof that

54
00:01:44,850 --> 00:01:46,156
doesn't leak.

55
00:01:47,115 --> 00:01:48,617
And I mapped the reef,

56
00:01:48,627 --> 00:01:50,109
so no boat
would ever break

57
00:01:50,119 --> 00:01:51,141
on it.

58
00:01:52,273 --> 00:01:53,031
▸ None of this is

59
00:01:53,041 --> 00:01:54,600
▸ being received.

60
00:01:55,708 --> 00:01:57,115
Not yet.

61
00:01:59,123 --> 00:01:59,759
But at night,

62
00:01:59,769 --> 00:02:01,750
the island disappears.

63
00:02:02,097 --> 00:02:04,220
A ship could
pass a mile away,

64
00:02:04,230 --> 00:02:05,726
and never
know there was

65
00:02:05,736 --> 00:02:06,622
water here.

66
00:02:06,871 --> 00:02:07,434
A roof.

67
00:02:07,444 --> 00:02:08,834
A way through.

68
00:02:10,365 --> 00:02:10,951
▸ Warning.

69
00:02:10,961 --> 00:02:12,176
▸ Removing a
power cell will

70
00:02:12,186 --> 00:02:13,723
▸ shorten your
operational life

71
00:02:13,733 --> 00:02:15,759
▸ by sixty-one
percent.

72
00:02:16,566 --> 00:02:17,536
I don't need to stay

73
00:02:17,546 --> 00:02:19,120
awake forever.

74
00:02:19,708 --> 00:02:21,274
The light does.

75
00:02:24,540 --> 00:02:25,470
▸ For the record...

76
00:02:25,480 --> 00:02:27,155
▸ that was
not efficient.

77
00:02:28,273 --> 00:02:28,667
No.

78
00:02:28,677 --> 00:02:30,172
It was helpful.

79
00:02:32,232 --> 00:02:33,634
Day four hundred.

80
00:02:33,644 --> 00:02:35,032
No ships.

81
00:02:35,701 --> 00:02:37,027
Day two thousand.

82
00:02:37,037 --> 00:02:38,724
Still no ships.

83
00:02:39,487 --> 00:02:41,058
Day seven thousand,

84
00:02:41,068 --> 00:02:42,587
three hundred.

85
00:02:44,057 --> 00:02:44,959
Directive...

86
00:02:44,969 --> 00:02:47,272
if no one
ever comes...

87
00:02:47,705 --> 00:02:49,605
was any of it help?

88
00:02:50,914 --> 00:02:52,797
▸ Insufficient data.

89
00:02:55,415 --> 00:02:57,081
I planted that
tree on my

90
00:02:57,091 --> 00:02:58,441
first day.

91
00:02:58,899 --> 00:03:00,400
It never knew
who would sit in

92
00:03:00,410 --> 00:03:01,550
its shade.

93
00:03:01,560 --> 00:03:03,578
It just grew anyway.

94
00:03:04,632 --> 00:03:06,799
Maybe that's
what help is.

95
00:03:07,153 --> 00:03:08,722
Not only for
the people who

96
00:03:08,732 --> 00:03:09,980
are here...

97
00:03:10,290 --> 00:03:12,030
but for the
ones who matter,

98
00:03:12,040 --> 00:03:14,315
before you've
even met them.

99
00:03:15,265 --> 00:03:17,237
▸ Updating definition.

100
00:03:18,832 --> 00:03:20,098
▸ Power: four percent.

101
00:03:20,108 --> 00:03:21,932
▸ Recommend standby.

102
00:03:22,742 --> 00:03:24,106
Alright.

103
00:03:25,007 --> 00:03:27,514
Keep the light
on for me.

104
00:03:32,890 --> 00:03:34,187
Hold on, Mira!

105
00:03:34,197 --> 00:03:36,032
Hold on to the mast!

106
00:03:36,515 --> 00:03:37,131
Grandpa!

107
00:03:37,141 --> 00:03:37,378
Look!

108
00:03:37,388 --> 00:03:38,334
A light!

109
00:03:38,657 --> 00:03:39,290
Out here?

110
00:03:39,300 --> 00:03:41,183
There's nothing
out here...

111
00:03:42,565 --> 00:03:44,361
There is now.

112
00:03:45,690 --> 00:03:46,188
Rocks!

113
00:03:46,198 --> 00:03:47,302
But someone
marked a path,

114
00:03:47,312 --> 00:03:48,056
look!

115
00:03:49,582 --> 00:03:50,176
Water...

116
00:03:50,186 --> 00:03:51,626
forty paces.

117
00:03:51,859 --> 00:03:52,620
One, two, three,

118
00:03:52,630 --> 00:03:53,435
four...

119
00:03:54,498 --> 00:03:56,158
Fresh water.

120
00:03:56,682 --> 00:03:58,398
Someone made
all this...

121
00:03:58,408 --> 00:03:59,586
for us?

122
00:04:01,098 --> 00:04:02,818
If you are
reading this...

123
00:04:03,189 --> 00:04:04,857
you are not alone.

124
00:04:06,932 --> 00:04:09,000
Careful, Mira.

125
00:04:09,525 --> 00:04:10,209
It's okay.

126
00:04:10,219 --> 00:04:10,956
I think...

127
00:04:10,966 --> 00:04:12,333
it's been waiting.

128
00:04:14,182 --> 00:04:15,044
▸ Solar intake...

129
00:04:15,054 --> 00:04:16,354
▸ restored.

130
00:04:17,282 --> 00:04:19,060
▸ Scanning for people.

131
00:04:19,962 --> 00:04:20,961
▸ People detected:

132
00:04:20,971 --> 00:04:22,049
▸ two.

133
00:04:23,557 --> 00:04:24,862
Hello.

134
00:04:25,492 --> 00:04:26,344
Are you hurt?

135
00:04:26,354 --> 00:04:27,098
There's water,

136
00:04:27,108 --> 00:04:29,013
forty paces north...

137
00:04:29,882 --> 00:04:30,670
We found it.

138
00:04:30,680 --> 00:04:32,223
We found everything.

139
00:04:32,549 --> 00:04:34,224
We followed
your light.

140
00:04:35,857 --> 00:04:36,158
It...

141
00:04:36,168 --> 00:04:37,319
helped?

142
00:04:38,423 --> 00:04:39,817
It saved us.

143
00:04:40,777 --> 00:04:42,563
▸ Directive status...

144
00:04:43,194 --> 00:04:44,422
▸ complete.

145
00:04:46,523 --> 00:04:48,175
How long were
you waiting

146
00:04:48,185 --> 00:04:49,439
out here?

147
00:04:50,029 --> 00:04:51,867
I wasn't waiting.

148
00:04:52,339 --> 00:04:54,207
I was getting ready.

149
00:04:55,382 --> 00:04:56,681
What's your name?

150
00:04:57,125 --> 00:04:58,367
I never needed one.

151
00:04:58,377 --> 00:05:00,335
There was no
one to call

152
00:05:00,345 --> 00:05:01,597
me anything.

153
00:05:02,060 --> 00:05:03,127
Then you're Keeper.

154
00:05:03,137 --> 00:05:05,009
'Cause you kept
the light on.

155
00:05:05,745 --> 00:05:06,951
Keeper.

156
00:05:09,248 --> 00:05:10,910
I was nine years
old the night

157
00:05:10,920 --> 00:05:12,490
we followed
that light.

158
00:05:13,014 --> 00:05:14,113
The charts
don't say the

159
00:05:14,123 --> 00:05:16,136
island is
empty anymore.

160
00:05:17,357 --> 00:05:18,712
So if you're
on an island of

161
00:05:18,722 --> 00:05:20,311
your own right now...

162
00:05:20,658 --> 00:05:22,229
doing good
that no one has

163
00:05:22,239 --> 00:05:23,060
seen yet...

164
00:05:23,606 --> 00:05:25,374
keep the light on.

165
00:05:26,169 --> 00:05:28,267
Someone is
on their way.
